            <ArticleTitle>[Differential diagnosis of headache and facial pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>193-200</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Headache and facial pain are frequent complaints. The underlying process is most often benign but serious conditions may be present requiring an urgent diagnostic approach. A careful history including psychologic evaluation and a meticulous neurologic examination are essential for an adequate selection of complementary laboratory testing.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
